  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 3: DDL & SAMPLE DATA ==================== -->
  <h1>3. Table Creation &amp; Key Constraints</h1>
  <p>
    The relational schema was created using <code>BIGINT</code> primary keys with <code>AUTO_INCREMENT</code> for high scalability and indexing performance. Foreign keys were defined with strict referential integrity rules (<code>ON UPDATE CASCADE</code>, <code>ON DELETE RESTRICT</code>) to prevent accidental record orphanages in administrative audit trails. <code>UNIQUE</code> constraints were enforced on citizen email addresses, department codes, grievance tracking IDs, and the 1:1 foreign key in feedback.
  </p>
  <p>
    The complete schema was verified in the MySQL 8.4 Command Line Client.
  </p>

  <h1>4. Sample Data Insertion</h1>
  <p>
    Sample civic records were inserted in <strong>foreign key safe order</strong>: <code>departments</code> &rarr; <code>users</code> &rarr; <code>grievances</code> &rarr; <code>resolution_logs</code> &rarr; <code>feedbacks</code>. The dataset mirrors realistic municipal scenarios including citizen accounts, designated GRO officers across municipal departments (Water Supply, Roads, Electricity, Sanitation, Public Health), complaint tickets with diverse priority levels, comprehensive resolution logs, and citizen evaluation ratings.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Expected Sample row counts after insertion:</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT 'departments' AS table_name, COUNT(*) AS records FROM departments</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">UNION ALL</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT 'users', COUNT(*) FROM users</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">UNION ALL</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT 'grievances', COUNT(*) FROM grievances</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">UNION ALL</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT 'resolution_logs', COUNT(*) FROM resolution_logs</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">UNION ALL</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT 'feedbacks', COUNT(*) FROM feedbacks;</span>
+-----------------+---------+
| table_name      | records |
+-----------------+---------+
| departments     |       5 |
| users           |       7 |
| grievances      |       6 |
| resolution_logs |       6 |
| feedbacks       |       4 |
+-----------------+---------+
<span class="t-count">5 rows in set (0.01 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 4: 5. JOIN OPERATIONS & 5.1 INNER JOIN ==================== -->
  <h1>5. JOIN OPERATIONS</h1>
  <p>
    Join operations were used to correlate related civic entities across normalized relational tables. In accordance with database best practices, explicit column selections and transparent table aliases are utilized to clearly illustrate foreign key relationships and maintain readability during practical assessment.
  </p>

  <h2>5.1 INNER JOIN</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> Returns only records that have matching values in both joined tables based on the join predicate. Citizens who have not yet submitted any grievance tickets, or orphaned grievances without valid citizen accounts, are omitted from the result set.
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">u.name AS citizen_name,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">u.phone_number,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.priority,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.status</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM users u</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INNER JOIN grievances g</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">ON u.id = g.citizen_id;</span>
+-----------------+--------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+----------+-------------+
| citizen_name    | phone_number | tracking_id   | subject                              | priority | status      |
+-----------------+--------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+----------+-------------+
| Ramesh Kumar    | 9876543210   | GRV-2026-0001 | Water pipeline burst in Anna Nagar   | HIGH     | RESOLVED    |
| Ramesh Kumar    | 9876543210   | GRV-2026-0002 | Low water pressure in 4th Cross      | LOW      | IN_PROGRESS |
| Priya Sharma    | 9845123456   | GRV-2026-0003 | Deep pothole on Outer Ring Road      | HIGH     | RESOLVED    |
| Priya Sharma    | 9845123456   | GRV-2026-0004 | Street light not working on MG Road  | MEDIUM   | RESOLVED    |
| Ananya Iyer     | 9731234567   | GRV-2026-0005 | Garbage dump overflow near market    | MEDIUM   | IN_PROGRESS |
| Vikram Singh    | 9900112233   | GRV-2026-0006 | Transformer sparking near bus stop   | HIGH     | PENDING     |
+-----------------+--------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+----------+-------------+
<span class="t-count">6 rows in set (0.00 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 5: 5.2 LEFT JOIN ==================== -->
  <h2>5.2 LEFT JOIN</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> Returns all rows from the left table (<code>departments</code>), plus matched rows from the right table (<code>grievances</code>). Where a department has no grievances currently assigned to it, the right-side columns return as <code>NULL</code>. This query is essential for municipal dashboards to identify inactive or complaint-free administrative units (e.g., Public Health Department).
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">d.name AS department_name,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">d.code,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.status</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM departments d</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">LEFT JOIN grievances g</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">ON d.id = g.department_id;</span>
+-----------------------------------+------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
| department_name                   | code | tracking_id   | subject                              | status      |
+-----------------------------------+------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
| Water Supply and Sewerage Board   | WSB  | GRV-2026-0001 | Water pipeline burst in Anna Nagar   | RESOLVED    |
| Water Supply and Sewerage Board   | WSB  | GRV-2026-0002 | Low water pressure in 4th Cross      | IN_PROGRESS |
| Roads and Infrastructure Dept     | RND  | GRV-2026-0003 | Deep pothole on Outer Ring Road      | RESOLVED    |
| Electricity and Power Board       | ELE  | GRV-2026-0004 | Street light not working on MG Road  | RESOLVED    |
| Solid Waste Management Dept       | SWM  | GRV-2026-0005 | Garbage dump overflow near market    | IN_PROGRESS |
| Electricity and Power Board       | ELE  | GRV-2026-0006 | Transformer sparking near bus stop   | PENDING     |
| Public Health and Sanitation Dept | PHD  | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>          | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>                                 | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>        |
+-----------------------------------+------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
<span class="t-count">7 rows in set (0.00 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 6: 5.3 RIGHT JOIN & 5.4 FULL JOIN ==================== -->
  <h2>5.3 RIGHT JOIN</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> Returns all rows from the right table (<code>grievances</code>), matched with records from the left table (<code>feedbacks</code>). When a grievance has not yet been resolved or the citizen has not yet submitted a review, all feedback fields evaluate to <code>NULL</code>.
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.status,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">f.rating,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">f.comment,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">f.is_appealed</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM feedbacks f</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">RIGHT JOIN grievances g</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">ON f.grievance_id = g.id;</span>
+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+--------+-------------------------------------+-------------+
| tracking_id   | subject                              | status      | rating | comment                             | is_appealed |
+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+--------+-------------------------------------+-------------+
| GRV-2026-0001 | Water pipeline burst in Anna Nagar   | RESOLVED    |      5 | Prompt response and clean repair    |           0 |
| GRV-2026-0002 | Low water pressure in 4th Cross      | IN_PROGRESS |   <span class="t-null">NULL</span> | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>                                |        <span class="t-null">NULL</span> |
| GRV-2026-0003 | Deep pothole on Outer Ring Road      | RESOLVED    |      4 | Pothole filled, road leveling fine  |           0 |
| GRV-2026-0004 | Street light not working on MG Road  | RESOLVED    |      2 | Light fixed but flickers at night   |           1 |
| GRV-2026-0005 | Garbage dump overflow near market    | IN_PROGRESS |   <span class="t-null">NULL</span> | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>                                |        <span class="t-null">NULL</span> |
| GRV-2026-0006 | Transformer sparking near bus stop   | PENDING     |   <span class="t-null">NULL</span> | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>                                |        <span class="t-null">NULL</span> |
+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+--------+-------------------------------------+-------------+
<span class="t-count">6 rows in set (0.00 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <h2>5.4 FULL JOIN (FULL OUTER JOIN)</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> Returns all rows from both right and left tables, displaying <code>NULL</code> on whichever side lacks a matching row. In MySQL 8.4, because <code>FULL OUTER JOIN</code> is not a single native keyword, it is syntactically implemented using a <code>LEFT JOIN</code> and <code>RIGHT JOIN</code> united with the <code>UNION</code> operator.
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">d.name AS department_name,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.status</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM departments d</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">LEFT JOIN grievances g ON d.id = g.department_id</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">UNION</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">d.name AS department_name,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.status</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM departments d</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">RIGHT JOIN grievances g ON d.id = g.department_id;</span>
+-----------------------------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
| department_name                   | tracking_id   | subject                              | status      |
+-----------------------------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
| Water Supply and Sewerage Board   | GRV-2026-0001 | Water pipeline burst in Anna Nagar   | RESOLVED    |
| Water Supply and Sewerage Board   | GRV-2026-0002 | Low water pressure in 4th Cross      | IN_PROGRESS |
| Roads and Infrastructure Dept     | GRV-2026-0003 | Deep pothole on Outer Ring Road      | RESOLVED    |
| Electricity and Power Board       | GRV-2026-0004 | Street light not working on MG Road  | RESOLVED    |
| Solid Waste Management Dept       | GRV-2026-0005 | Garbage dump overflow near market    | IN_PROGRESS |
| Electricity and Power Board       | GRV-2026-0006 | Transformer sparking near bus stop   | PENDING     |
| Public Health and Sanitation Dept | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>          | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>                                 | <span class="t-null">NULL</span>        |
+-----------------------------------+---------------+--------------------------------------+-------------+
<span class="t-count">7 rows in set (0.01 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 7: 5.5 NATURAL JOIN ==================== -->
  <h2>5.5 NATURAL JOIN</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> Automatically joins two tables on all columns that share identical column names across schemas—without specifying an explicit <code>ON</code> condition. MySQL compares every identically named column and returns rows where all shared column values are identical.
  </p>
  <p>
    In normalized relational schemas where tables independently define columns such as <code>id</code> (primary key), a NATURAL JOIN attempts to match <code>grievances.id = resolution_logs.id</code>. Because these identifiers represent unrelated auto-increment counters across independent tables, the query produces an empty set. This intentionally tests and demonstrates why explicit <code>ON</code> predicates are essential for production systems.
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">subject,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">action_taken</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM grievances</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">NATURAL JOIN resolution_logs;</span>
<span class="t-count">Empty set (0.00 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <!-- ==================== PAGE 8: MULTI-TABLE JOIN & ERROR TESTING ==================== -->
  <h2>5.6 MULTI-TABLE AUDIT JOIN (Citizens, Complaints, Departments &amp; GRO Officers)</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Description:</strong> A comprehensive 4-table join representing the end-to-end municipal governance workflow: correlating the citizen who filed the grievance, the assigned department, the handling GRO officer, and the recorded resolution action.
  </p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">SELECT</span> 
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">g.tracking_id,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">c.name AS citizen,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">d.code AS dept,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">gro.name AS officer,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">rl.action_taken,</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span>     <span class="cmd">rl.logged_at</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">FROM grievances g</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INNER JOIN users c ON g.citizen_id = c.id</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INNER JOIN departments d ON g.department_id = d.id</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INNER JOIN resolution_logs rl ON rl.grievance_id = g.id</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INNER JOIN users gro ON rl.gro_id = gro.id</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">ORDER BY rl.logged_at DESC;</span>
+---------------+--------------+------+--------------------+-----------------------------+---------------------+
| tracking_id   | citizen      | dept | officer            | action_taken                | logged_at           |
+---------------+--------------+------+--------------------+-----------------------------+---------------------+
| GRV-2026-0004 | Priya Sharma | ELE  | Sri Arvind Nair    | Replaced LED Luminaire      | 2026-03-02 11:30:00 |
| GRV-2026-0003 | Priya Sharma | RND  | Smt. Kavitha Reddy | Filled pothole with cold mix| 2026-03-02 09:15:00 |
| GRV-2026-0001 | Ramesh Kumar | WSB  | Dr. Rajesh Verma   | Replaced burst section pipe | 2026-03-01 16:45:00 |
| GRV-2026-0005 | Ananya Iyer  | SWM  | Smt. Kavitha Reddy | Dispatched municipal truck  | 2026-03-01 14:00:00 |
| GRV-2026-0002 | Ramesh Kumar | WSB  | Dr. Rajesh Verma   | Inspected booster pumps     | 2026-03-01 11:00:00 |
| GRV-2026-0001 | Ramesh Kumar | WSB  | Dr. Rajesh Verma   | Initial emergency isolation | 2026-03-01 08:30:00 |
+---------------+--------------+------+--------------------+-----------------------------+---------------------+
<span class="t-count">6 rows in set (0.01 sec)</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <h1>6. Intentional SQL Error Testing &amp; Constraint Debugging</h1>
  <p>
    As demonstrated in the reference practical, intentional SQL errors were executed to validate that foreign keys and domain integrity constraints actively prevent corrupt or inconsistent state transitions.
  </p>

  <h2>6.1 Foreign Key Constraint Violation (Error 1452)</h2>
  <p>Attempting to insert a grievance for a non-existent citizen (<code>citizen_id = 9999</code>):</p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INSERT INTO grievances (tracking_id, subject, description, status, priority, citizen_id, department_id, created_at)</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">VALUES ('GRV-TEST-FAIL', 'Illegal Waste Dumping', 'Waste dumped near lake', 'PENDING', 'HIGH', 9999, 1, NOW());</span>
<span class="t-err">ERROR 1452 (23000): Cannot add or update a child row: a foreign key constraint fails (`grievance_db`.`grievances`, CONSTRAINT `fk_grievance_citizen` FOREIGN KEY (`citizen_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`))</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <h2>6.2 Duplicate Key Entry Violation (Error 1062)</h2>
  <p>Attempting to insert a duplicate unique department code (<code>code = 'WSB'</code>):</p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INSERT INTO departments (name, code, description, created_at)</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">VALUES ('Water Services Agency', 'WSB', 'Duplicate department code test', NOW());</span>
<span class="t-err">ERROR 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry 'WSB' for key 'departments.code'</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

  <h2>6.3 Check Constraint Violation (Error 3819)</h2>
  <p>Attempting to submit citizen feedback with a rating outside the permitted 1&ndash;5 range (<code>rating = 7</code>):</p>

  <div class="terminal"><span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">INSERT INTO feedbacks (grievance_id, rating, comment, is_appealed, submitted_at)</span>
    <span class="prompt">-&gt;</span> <span class="cmd">VALUES (1, 7, 'Invalid rating score test', 0, NOW());</span>
<span class="t-err">ERROR 3819 (HY000): Check constraint 'chk_feedback_rating' is violated.</span>

<span class="prompt">mysql&gt;</span></div>

</div>
